From: (local patch, not an upstream commit) QM1 Debian Maintainers <qm1-debian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: allow key removal when the CAM table is full

Carried from the upstream rtw-next commit

  b60ee9891e400eeae64053716a8e839e2f6d137c
  "wifi: rtw88: allow key removal when the CAM table is full"
  (Hungyu Lin, 2026-10-19)

which is *not* part of the upstream snapshot this module is built from
(05441d697f7f9a927264f4058cbbc6a03dfcac9d, a torvalds/linux master
snapshot of 2026-11-03): master only merged rtw-next up to the
"rtw-next-2026-10-08" tag, so every 8723B fix from 2026-10-09 onwards
is missing from the tree we ship.

Why we carry it:

rtw_ops_set_key() looked for a free CAM entry before it looked at
the command.  Once every pairwise entry was in use, DISABLE_KEY returned
-ENOSPC without clearing the entry that was already there, so the old
key could never be removed from the hardware (for example when the AP
rekeys, or when we reconnect after the link dropped).

The upstream fix allocates the CAM entry only for SET_KEY; DISABLE_KEY
reuses the existing key->hw_key_idx.
diff --git a/mac80211.c b/mac80211.c
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -598,20 +598,20 @@
 
 	rtw_leave_lps_deep(rtwdev);
 
-	if (key->flags & IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_PAIRWISE) {
-		hw_key_idx = rtw_sec_get_free_cam(sec);
-	} else {
-		/* multiple interfaces? */
-		hw_key_idx = key->keyidx;
-	}
-
-	if (hw_key_idx >= sec->total_cam_num) {
-		ret = -ENOSPC;
-		goto out;
-	}
-
 	switch (cmd) {
 	case SET_KEY:
+		if (key->flags & IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_PAIRWISE) {
+			hw_key_idx = rtw_sec_get_free_cam(sec);
+		} else {
+			/* multiple interfaces? */
+			hw_key_idx = key->keyidx;
+		}
+
+		if (hw_key_idx >= sec->total_cam_num) {
+			ret = -ENOSPC;
+			goto out;
+		}
+
 		/* need sw generated IV */
 		key->flags |= IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_GENERATE_IV;
 		key->hw_key_idx = hw_key_idx;
